---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/**
 * FACTUAL, NOT INFLATED — deliberately.
 *
 * Google Ads' Unacceptable Business Practices rule bans "an inaccurate business
 * name that does not clearly represent the advertised business" and "a
 * fictitious business that lacks the qualifications or capacity to provide the
 * advertised products or services", enforced by suspension on detection,
 * without warning, permanently. Meta cross-references this page against
 * Business Verification documents.
 *
 * iGrowFast LLC is a real Wyoming entity, so verification itself is truthful.
 * The entire risk lives in the copy. So this page describes what the PRODUCT
 * does and who it is for — never how large, old, or established the company is.
 * No founder names. No invented history, headcount, or customer counts. The
 * Sheridan address is the registered address and is never called an office.
 * German processing is stated plainly rather than implied away.
 */
---

<Base
  title="About — iGrowFast"
  description="iGrowFast LLC builds operational software for cash-on-delivery e-commerce: orders, carriers, chat, ad spend and reconciliation in one workspace."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="head">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>We build the workspace COD actually needs</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Cash-on-delivery is not a payment method bolted onto normal e-commerce.
        It is a different business, and it breaks the tools built for card
        checkout.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="body">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The problem we work on</h2>
        <p>
          In a COD business the order isn't finished when someone clicks buy. It
          is finished when a courier hands over a package and collects cash —
          days later, sometimes at the third attempt, sometimes never. Between
          those two moments sit a chat thread, a courier portal, an ad campaign
          that produced the lead, and a commission that someone has to calculate
          correctly.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most teams run that on a spreadsheet and ten browser tabs. It works
          until it doesn't — and it stops working exactly when the business
          starts growing, which is the worst possible moment.
        </p>
        <p>
          iGrowFast puts the loop in one place: orders and their real status,
          the couriers you already use, the numbers you already sell on, the ad
          spend that produced the order, and a ledger that tracks and reconciles
          what everyone is owed.
        </p>

        <h2>How we think about it</h2>
        <p>
          Money has to be right. A tool that is merely fast, but quietly wrong
          about a commission, is worse than the spreadsheet it replaced. The
          reconciliation is the part we are most careful about.
        </p>
        <p>
          Roles see their own slice. A media buyer sees the campaigns they run
          and the commission they earned — not another team's margins. That
          isn't a setting; it's how the system is built.
        </p>
        <p>
          Density with hierarchy. Operators need a lot on screen. That is a
          reason to design carefully, not a reason to ship a wall of grey.
        </p>

        <h2>The company</h2>
        <p>
          iGrowFast is operated by <strong>iGrowFast LLC</strong>, a Wyoming
          limited liability company registered in the United States. Our
          registered address is below.
        </p>
        <p>
          The platform runs on infrastructure located in <strong>Germany</strong>,
          and customer data is stored and processed in Europe. We say that plainly
          here because it belongs in an honest description of the business, not
          only in a privacy policy — see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
          for exactly what is processed and where.
        </p>
        <p>
          The product is used today by cash-on-delivery businesses operating in
          Morocco, and its interface is primarily French. We are not going to
          pretend to be bigger or older than we are.
        </p>

        <address>
          <strong>iGrowFast LLC</strong><br />
          30 N Gould St Ste R<br />
          Sheridan, WY 82801<br />
          United States
        </address>
        <p class="fine">
          That is our registered address. It is not a walk-in office — if you
          want to reach us, <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and a person will
          answer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Want to see whether it fits?</h2>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Talk to us</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 5rem) 0;
  }
  .head h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-hero);
    line-height: 1.05;
    max-width: 20ch;
  }
  .lede {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step-body-lg);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .body {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 1rem + 4vw, 4rem);
  }
  .narrow {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  address {
    font-style: normal;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-block: 1.5rem 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .fine {
    font-size: var(--step-small);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .close {
    padding-block: var(--space-section);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .close h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
</style>
